RIMENTS / REAL BEHAVIOR')}<div class=\"section-heading\"><h2>Go on.<br><i>Touch the controls.</i></h2><p>Design is a set of decisions.<br>Move one. See what changes.</p></div><div class=\"playground\"><div class=\"control-list\"><label>Type scale<input id=\"type-scale\" type=\"range\" min=\"28\" max=\"66\" value=\"48\"></label><label>Spacing<input id=\"spacing\" type=\"range\" min=\"18\" max=\"60\" value=\"40\"></label><label>Preview width<input id=\"preview-width\" type=\"range\" min=\"280\" max=\"850\" value=\"850\"></label><label>Contrast<select id=\"contrast\"><option value=\"light\">Light / forest</option><option value=\"dark\">Dark / bone</option></select></label><button id=\"play-reset\">Reset composition ↺</button></div><div class=\"play-preview\" id=\"play-preview\"><div class=\"play-meta\"><span>GALILEA / INTERFACE STUDY</span><span>01</span></div><h3 id=\"play-title\">A shared place.<br>An open invitation.</h3><p>Small details make a system feel easier to use. This is a real responsive composition, not an image.</p></div></div><div class=\"architecture-nodes\" id=\"architecture\">${['Browser','API gateway','Authentication','Data service','Response'].map((x,i)=>`<button data-node=\"${i}\" aria-pressed=\"${i===0}\">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / ${x}</button>`).join('')}</div><p class=\"architecture-note\" id=\"architecture-note\"></p></section><section id=\"experiments\">${sectionLabel('04','SELECTED EXPERIMENTS','CONCEPTS / WORKING STUDIES')}<div class=\"section-heading\"><h2>Room for<br><i>the unexpected.</i></h2><p>A few small studies beyond the usual boundaries of a web project.</p></div><div class=\"experiments-list\"><article class=\"experiment\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">01 / KINETIC TYPOGRAPHY — CONCEPT</span><div class=\"type-demo\" id=\"type-demo\">Make room.</div><label class=\"eyebrow\" for=\"letter-space\">Change the rhythm</label><input id=\"letter-space\" type=\"range\" min=\"-5\" max=\"12\" value=\"-3\"><p>Spacing changes the voice of a phrase. A restrained, keyboard-accessible type study.</p></article><article class=\"experiment\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">02 / DOCUMENT SYSTEMS — DEMONSTRATION</span><h3>Information needs a hierarchy.</h3><p>An illustrative starting scenario and a structured report layout.</p><div class=\"comparison\"><div>weekly report<br>assets 51 done 31<br>check pump location<br>next inspection friday</div><div class=\"after\"><b>FIELD REVIEW</b><hr>31 / 51 verified<br><br><b>Next action</b><br>Confirm pump location.</div></div></article><article class=\"experiment\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">03 / PRESENTATION — DEMONSTRATION</span><h3>One thought. Enough space.</h3><p>A presentation study that adapts to a fullscreen display.</p><button id=\"presentation-open\" style=\"margin-top:20px\">Open presentation ↗</button></article><article class=\"experiment\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">04 / WORKFLOW — CONCEPT</span><h3>A smaller, clearer community.</h3><p>A Discord information architecture study: announcements, shared chat, and temporary two-person voice rooms. This is a workflow concept, not a connected bot.</p><details style=\"margin-top:20px\"><summary>Inspect the workflow</summary><p>Join a voice lobby → bot creates a private room → cap at two members → remove room when empty. Permissions and bot hosting still require implementation.</p></details></article></div></section><section id=\"profile\">${sectionLabel('05','THE HUMAN BEHIND THE SYSTEM','KEVIN SIMATUPANG')}<div class=\"profile-grid\"><div><div class=\"profile-mark\">k↗</div><span class=\"mono\">BASED IN BALIKPAPAN<br>EAST KALIMANTAN, INDONESIA</span></div><div class=\"profile-copy\"><h2>Curiosity.<br><i>With structure.</i></h2><p>I like the moment a complicated process starts making sense. Sometimes that means a website. Sometimes it is a spreadsheet, a better workflow, or a detail nobody noticed until it worked.</p><dl><div><dt>CURRENT EMPLOYMENT</dt><dd>PT. Wulandari Bangun Laksana<br>February 2026 — Present</dd></div><div><dt>EA